'' T46, RUN: text passed through 'base( ... )' arrives intact. The base path had its own
'' argument loop, which knew a byref UDT and a byref wstring but not a string: a variable
'' went over as its loaded descriptor and clang refused the call, a literal reached the
'' base empty, and a parameter left to its default dropped the statement. It now uses
'' PushCtorArgs_, as every other constructor call does. Also covers the wstring and byref
'' UDT arguments that path rerouted. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win64-msvc tests/codegen/src/base-call-string.bas -o tests/codegen/basecallstring.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/basecallstring.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/basecallstring.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: variable 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: literal 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: expression! 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: wide text
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: pt 3,4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: by value
